==============================================================================================================
DERIVATION
==============================================================================================================
A + B = 1

At theta = pi/4:

A' = A cos(theta) + B sin(theta)
   = (A+B)/sqrt(2)
   = 1/sqrt(2)

The quadratic efficiency law gives:

f_c = sqrt(eta)
    = sqrt(3/5)

Therefore:

P_geo = f_c / A'
      = sqrt(3/5) / (1/sqrt(2))
      = sqrt(3/5) * sqrt(2)
      = sqrt(6/5)

